<title>SRI LANKA: CRICKET-INDIA V PAKISTAN ASIA CUP MATCH CALLED OFF.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-INDIA V PAKISTAN ASIA CUP MATCH CALLED OFF.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asia Cup match between India and Pakistan at Colombo's Singhalese Sports Club was called off on Sunday due to poor light.</p>
<p>Pakistan were 30 for 5 in nine overs when play was finally stopped after an earlier interruption due to rain.</p>
<p>The match, which will decide who meets Sri Lanka in the final on July 26, will be replayed on Monday.</p>
</text>
